Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 00:05:49 +0200
Subject: arm64: dts: qcom: dragon-q8b: describe the HDMI bridge supply timing

The CH7218A only samples the EDID of its sink while booting, so it has
to be restarted to see a new one, and this rail is the only way in: it
feeds the regulator making the converter's 3.3V, and the reset hangs
off an RC on that 3.3V with a time constant near a hundred
milliseconds. Hold it down long enough to discharge, and up long enough
for the firmware load and the DDC read that follow.

Drop regulator-boot-on: it pins the rail enabled for the whole uptime,
so the bridge can never take it down.

Signed-off-by: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-radxa-dragon-q8b.dts | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-radxa-dragon-q8b.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-radxa-dragon-q8b.dts
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-radxa-dragon-q8b.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-radxa-dragon-q8b.dts
@@ -401,12 +401,11 @@ vcc_5v_s: regulator-vcc-5v-s {
 
 		gpio = <&tlmm 159 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 		enable-active-high;
-		startup-delay-us = <33000>;
+		startup-delay-us = <250000>;
+		off-on-delay-us = <150000>;
 
 		pinctrl-0 = <&vcc_5v_s_reg_en>;
 		pinctrl-names = "default";
-
-		regulator-boot-on;
 	};
 
 	vcc_nvme_3v3: regulator-vcc-nvme-3v3 {
